  "findings": [
    "Rebuilt by the LilScript compiler at d1d48c4c (finer/059-idiom-directed-naming, M4.1 nominal identity); the released dist of 55c34b5 rebuilds byte for byte with it, so every size change below is the port source.",
    "Port source only, no compiler change: src/entry.lil exports the public API only (the official Jest suites get their internal modules from a separate test entry, test/katex.lil, compiled into dist/katex.test.js), so the compiler sees the real export surface; the build no longer filters an export list.",
    "Contrib sources spelled as upstream writes them: bare document/window/console/Element/Text/RegExp externs instead of globalThis reads; mhchem logical operators through JS.or/JS.and and its thirteen key loops as for-in; render-a11y-string lookup tables as object literals and method-call pushes; auto-render copies options with for-in plus hasOwnProperty and calls preProcess as a method; copy-tex uses instanceof through a three-line module the compiler embeds (lilscript.copy-tex.toml).",
    "The site measures SWC 1.16.2 over the published graph and over the Flow-source bundle, defines __VERSION__ in the Flow-source lanes (the Terser lane used to throw on import), and requires every lane to import and render a formula before it is measured.",
    "katex.cjs, katex.umd.js, katex.min.js and the contrib .cjs/.min.js files are esbuild re-bundles of the compiler ESM, not compiler-written (plan M12.2)."
  ],
